openmediavault-notifier (8.1.0) stable; urgency=low

  * Move the notifier settings to their own page under
    System > Notification > Notifier.
  * Replace only the stock emails to the administrator addresses, mail to
    other users is delivered as usual. The switch takes effect when the
    configuration is applied.
  * Restore the stock emails when the plugin is removed, and print the
    recovery commands if the Postfix configuration cannot be updated.
  * Ignore the email channel's own messages, they looped with a local SMTP
    server.
  * Send the default email recipients a single copy with a local SMTP server.
  * Classify monit, file system, UPS, I/O error, virus alert, virus scan,
    USB backup and update report messages.
  * Decode encoded subjects and keep bracketed subject prefixes.
  * Escape Slack markup and suppress Discord mentions.
  * Keep delivering to the other channels when one channel fails.
  * Run the channel test as the notification user.
  * Write the SMTP password only when an email channel is enabled.
  * Require openmediavault 8.0.5-2 or later, older releases drop all
    outgoing mail.

 -- Rui Almeida <rui.almeida011@gmail.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:59:09 +0100

